{
  "_comment": [
    "IBC routes we care about, taken from the Cosmos chain registry's _IBC",
    "directory (github.com/cosmos/chain-registry/_IBC). Those files are the",
    "canonical pairing: a chain can carry several channels to the same",
    "counterparty, most of them long dead, and only the registry says which one",
    "is the live path.",
    "",
    "Both chainIds must exist in config/chains for a route to render — each side",
    "is probed against its own chain's endpoints.",
    "",
    "AtomOne <-> gno.land is deliberately absent: gno.land runs Tendermint2 with",
    "no IBC module, so no such channel exists to describe. It can be added the",
    "day one does."
  ],

